<title>USA: US Senate bill sets 3.8 bln board feet timber sale.</title>
<headline>US Senate bill sets 3.8 bln board feet timber sale.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bill passed Friday by a U.S. Senate subcommittee provides funds to cover 3.8 billion board feet of timber sales from national forests next fiscal year.</p>
<p>Of that, 2.525 billion board feet would be from green sales and 1.275 billion board feet from salvage, documents on a fiscal 1998 spending bill passed by the Senate Interior Appropriations subcommittee said.</p>
<p>That is the same as the administration's estimate for fiscal 1998 Forest Service timber sales, which would be down from this year's estimated 4.2 billion board feet and up from 1996's 3.4 billion board feet.</p>
<p>-- Washington newsroom, ((202-898-8300))</p>
